      "statusChangeID": "5d3fe0d92cef1344d9960e6b",
      "statusChangeNewStatus": "complete",
      "value": "Addressed with some changes to default VRC_PlayerAudioOverride component in an upcoming build. See notes: \n\nThis is due to some interactions between the override regions, our defaults (no regions present), and how Audio Sources work without ONSP/VRC_SpatialAudioSource.\n\nWe've changed the default settings in the VRC_PlayerAudioOverride component to Far: 40m, Near: 40m, and Volumetric Radius: 40m. This was done to match our no-regions-present default. This should prevent the odd behavior as noted.\n\nI will add two things:\n\n- These numbers are limits, and not boosts. This is an important distinction.\n\n- We strongly recommend using VRC_SpatialAudioSource with all avatar-based Audio Sources.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2019-07-27T05:15:14.948Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "When an avatar with an audio source with an ONSPAudioSource component enters a VRC_Player Audio Override region with the default settings for avatar audio, the audio seems to become quieter. This should not happen, as the documentation states that these settings are the default that is applied when no VRC_Player Audio Override is in effect.\n\nONSPAudioSourceのあるアバター音源が、アバター音源設定がデフォルトのままのVRC_Player Audio Overrideに入ると、音が小さくなる。資料によると、このデフォルト値はどのVRC_Player Audio Overrideに入ってない状態と同じ値のはずなので、この現象はバグだと思われます。\n\nSample video: https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=MsS-ZE8H-lA&feature=youtu.be\nTest world: https://www.vrchat.net/home/world/wrld_03f17561-5b91-4472-90e6-4ef148da2d6b\nAudio configuration: First image in https://twitter.com/Aetoriz_in_VR/status/1154976117389848576",
